# The repo root ignores `*.onnx` so nobody commits a trained model by accident.
# These graphs are the deliberate exception: they are a few hundred bytes each
# and they *are* the model-parity gate (ADR-0019). The gate compares Rust
# against a frozen Python answer, so the artifacts have to live in the tree —
# regenerating them next to the assertion would prove nothing.
!*.onnx
